bevy-horizon: give helper lanes zero from global loads (NAK_DEBUG=hzero)

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at 953fa75a, after 0001-0031. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it; this text before the first
"diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

A fragment shader runs a 2x2 quad of lanes at a time, and the lanes outside the triangle run as
helpers so that derivatives work. Helper lanes load from global memory only once bit 3 of
gr_gpcs_tpcs_sm_disp_ctrl is clear. NVK clears it with its SET_PRIV_REG macro, which Horizon
doesn't offer (nvk_cmd_draw.c), so on the Switch a helper lane's load leaves its destination
register as it was. Storage buffers are global memory, and Bevy's clustered forward lighting
loops over point and spot lights between bounds it loads from one, so in a helper lane those
loops can run for as long as a stale register says, and the channel times out (fifo idle
timeout). That is the GPU hang that Bevy's lit StandardMaterial caused on the Switch (sk8
findings 55 and 59): capping each loop at 16 iterations stopped it, while the pixels on screen
saw no lights at all.

With hzero, every global load in a fragment shader is followed by a select that gives helper
lanes zero, so such a loop runs no iterations in them. A helper lane's values reach the other
lanes only through derivatives, which a stale register spoils as surely. A shader without a
demote reads the helper state once (S2R of SR_THREAD_KILL); one with a demote reads it at each
load, as a demoted lane becomes a helper. Switch builds turn hzero on with the other defaults
(patch 0019); NAK_DEBUG=-hzero turns it off. The flags key NVK's shader cache, so shaders
compiled with and without it are cached apart.

On the host NAK (GM20B, the Switch defaults), Bevy 0.18's lit forward shader gains one select
per loaded value, 48, and one S2R, at the same 72 registers; Skate 3's world shader gains 34-188
instructions (3-7 %) at the same registers and about the same static cycle count. On the
console, Skate 3's test world, whose lit StandardMaterial ground hung the GPU in every earlier
build, runs at 30-40 fps with hzero (sk8 0.1.4-visfix10); with NAK_DEBUG=-hzero the same build
hangs again, and a retail map plays as it did without the patch.

